					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-29 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>Whatup y&#39;all this is daps, just to let you know - it&#39;s over - I got blog access! And now, nothin&#39; but the Cavi pics:<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/178/373800227_44d3be6ab7.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Put a mole on Condaleeza and you get Philippine Pres. GMA <br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/142/373800299_447033d78c.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />ML forum members maharlika (black jacket) and Nam (center) are so excited to be there.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/160/373800341_28f1d866fb.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />ML Forum member The Olaf prepares to belt out the chants<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/136/373800395_0d61a8880f.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />ML Forum member sincere9 is in this pic if you can find him<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/123/373800446_e8bca7cd7a.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Represent.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/147/373800499_ca001ecbf9.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />The nice weather provided a beautiful backdrop to the rally<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/143/373800538_b1bc857a0f.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Khingz is always tryin to start new fashion trends...here he is with the half-jacket-on look<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/154/373800569_5786b0d7cb.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />That sums it all up right there<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/159/373800617_dfe807d422.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Lt. Ehren Watada: &quot;You guys know when that Lovework is droppin&#39;&quot;?<br /><br />This was only the beginning for some of our Massline heroes. Geo, Abyssinian Creole (w/DJ WD4D), Sincere, Nam and a bunch of us other troublemakers trekked down to Tacoma immediately to prepare for the show. The Venue? Hell&#39;s Kitchen, home to many punk/metal shows, but also home to the most hospitable and professional staffs I&#39;ve seen yet. Thanks again guys...shouts out to Flash, cuz that&#39;s a jillthy nickname.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/98/373809292_f0b4a5d8bf.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />It&#39;s goin&#39; down!<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/98/373809316_8684f09f59.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />&quot;We&#39;re so excited to be here&quot;<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/188/373809367_6ad250a810.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />I love these guys!<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/149/373809565_b0bdfb6ed3.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />RA&#39;s next EP will be entitled &quot;Head Rap&quot;<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/160/373809524_5ea1bc6f66.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />North-by-northwest classic.<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/140/373809623_c0a5b453b8.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Both shows sold-out (of tickets, that is)<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/126/373809682_b217dcc798.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />&quot;MTV, where you been???&quot;<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/171/373809451_e0abe40628.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />These emcees sure like to point, dont they<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/177/373809419_42b6fe2cf1.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Almost the same shot (sagaba remix)<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/177/373809655_386f781f5b.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />&quot;Can I get a massage after this?&quot;<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/179/373809342_a20504327d.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Both are the future, son!<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/168/373809498_576252a5c5.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="263" /><br />Look, basically, we were at the club from 4:30pm-2:00am, ok? Big ups to Faith for cooking and having us over after. We love the two five trey.<br /><br />peace<br />dj daps1<br /> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-29 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>what a beautiful weekend, in so many ways.&nbsp; on saturday, masses of northwest folkers joined a nation-wide demonstration in <strong>protest</strong> of US involvement in iraq.&nbsp;&nbsp; the message&nbsp;to military recruiters was delivered loud and clear as the congregation assembled&nbsp;at the&nbsp;station&#39;s front door, <strong>like&nbsp;what?!?</strong>&nbsp; i send a special thank you to all in attendance for speaking in my absence - i love your work.&nbsp; aiyo <strong>daps</strong>, post some pics, sun.<br /><br />after the rally, a good grip of the company rolled south to attend church at <strong>hell&#39;s kitchen</strong>.&nbsp; news cameras from <strong>MTV</strong>, <strong>al&nbsp;jazeera</strong> and&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Japanes News Channel</strong> were intently focused&nbsp;on the evening&#39;s key note speaker,&nbsp;<strong>lt. ehren watada</strong>.&nbsp; he delivered a stirring speech, insisting that, if convicted and sentenced, his time served will have been a worthy sacrifice.&nbsp; that&#39;s a good look, my friend.&nbsp; another special thank you to the staff at hell&#39;s kitchen and to the entire<strong> 253</strong> for the support.&nbsp; aiyo daps, post some pics, sun.<br /><br />this weekend also marked the grand opening of <strong>silver platters</strong> in lower queen anne.&nbsp; for those of you who not familiar, the locally-owned mom-and-pop record shop moved into the house that tower built.&nbsp; i see the move as a remarkable success for independent music stores, in general.&nbsp; i highly encourage you all to purchase your copy of <strong>lovework</strong> at a silver platters near you.<br /><br />lastly, i capped off the weekend at a&nbsp;send-off party for the homie <strong>b-shorty</strong> (soon to be known to the entire fox-watching&nbsp;population as &quot;<strong>blake lewis</strong>&quot;).&nbsp; until watching him perform for a packed house at nectar, i had&nbsp;forgotten just how brilliant this kid is.&nbsp; we wish you much luck, much love, and the strength of a thousand soldiers, cousin -- you&#39;re gonna need it.<br /><br />be good, family...<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-25 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>* The military cost of 2.5 days of in Iraq would have provided college tuition for 463,000 low income students<br /><br />* The total war cost of $360 Billion would have paid for 17 Million full-ride scholarships to college<br /><br />This aint no theory or politics, just raw facts. And the fact is it&#39;s about to be FOUR YEARS since the illegal invasion and occupation of Iraq and almost FIVE YEARS since military occupation of Afghanistan and the Philippines, all under the guise of &quot;war on terrorism.&quot; With over 3,000 US casualites (and 650,000  Iraqi civilian casualties), Bush, Jr. is pledging 20,000 more troops to this madness. We need more folks to stand up like <strong>Lieutenant Ehren Watada</strong>, who faces a February 5 court-martial for refusing to deploy.<br /><br />We salute Lt. Watada for calling the war&#39;s legality and morality into question and refusing to follow unjust orders. As his court martial approaches, the urgency to  bring the troops back home increases daily. Saturday, January 27 marks a nationwide day of protest with a massive march on Washington. In solidarity, Seattle will be holding a rally and march at 1pm in the Central District. Lt. Watada and other guest speakers will be speaking at the Seattle rally. <br /><br />Later that evening, the entire Massline Fam (Blue Scholars, Common Market, Gabriel Teodros w/ Khingz Makoma and DJ daps1) will be rocking two shows (5pm - all-ages, 9pm - 21+) in <strong>Tacoma (Hell&#39;s Kitchen)</strong> in support of Lt. Watada&#39;s speaking campaign against the war. Special guest speakers, including Lt. Watada himself and the <strong>Bayan-USA</strong>homie <strong>Rachel Cendana</strong> will be at the show as well. See you there! (More info posted on the right in the EVENTS section).<br /><br />-----------------<br /><br />DEMONSTRATE to BRING THE TROOPS HOME NOW!<br /><br />When: 1:00PM <br />Where: Gather at <strong>21st &amp; Union</strong>, at the Center for Social Justice (The formerly the Dixon Campaign Headquarters), followed by a march to protest the military recruiting center, then onto Langston Hughes Center in nonviolent demonstration against the war in Iraq.<br /><br />More info: <a href="http://www.seattleactivism.org/events/event5460.htm">www.seattleactivism.org</a><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-23 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>big fat news for my big fat MassLine fam.<br /><br />MassLine is sponsoring its first ever comedy show produced by our good friend <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong>. this <strong>Friday, Jan. 26th</strong> at the <strong>Langston Hughes Performing Arts Center</strong> will be a night of social commentary mixed with absolute hilarity starring <strong>Ahamefule Oluo</strong>, <strong>Dan Moore</strong>, and <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong>.  the night will be hosted by yours truly and your boy <strong>Khalil</strong>, better known to some as <strong>Khingz of Abyssinian Creole</strong>.  <br /><br />this is an event that&#39;s a part of a week-long comedy festival , aka the <strong>Week Of Fun</strong>, put together by a group of local Seattle comics.  <br /><br />this event is especially special especially because it will also be the premier showing of the first <strong>MassLine ShortFilm &quot;Manoj.&quot;</strong> written by <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong> and directed by <strong>Zia Mohajerjasbi</strong>, <strong>&quot;Manoj&quot;</strong> is a 15 minute pseudo-documentary exploring the intricate details of the life and career of a pseudo-famous South Asian stand-up comedian.<br /><br />you can buy your tickets at <strong><a href="http://www.brownpapertickets.com/">BROWNPAPERTICKETS</a></strong> and we suggest you do that <strong>NOW</strong>.  only 7 bucks!<br /><br />saba<br /><br /><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/OuCaktPdSCo"><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/OuCaktPdSCo"></param><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param></object> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-22 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>white house press secretary <strong>tony snow&nbsp;</strong>(no yayo)&nbsp;announced this morning that a recent upsurge in violence in iraq is the result of a desperate attempt&nbsp;by insurgents to gain media attention, which is viewed as a &quot;major success.&quot;&nbsp; brilliant idea to have the PRESS SECRETARY make this statement - it&#39;s a testament to the american mantra: &quot;<strong>these colors don&#39;t run</strong>,&quot;&nbsp;in fact they&#39;re quite vivid&nbsp;on a wall-mounted 50-inch plasma screen...<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> [47] <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[5